From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cowboy Coder <howdy@cowboycoderhq.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:42:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Server: foreign drafter opt-in, automatic prefix cache, agent
 fixes

- FORGE_FOREIGN_DRAFTER=1 skips only the export-name pairing check, so the
  published DFlash2 drafter can draft for Bonsai (taps / T / shapes still checked).
- Automatic prefix cache: snapshots carry their own KV rows (segments past their
  parent prefix) in an LRU RAM tier (--prefix-cache-mb) with an SSD tier
  (--prefix-cache-disk-gb). System prompts are recorded and prefilled at startup
  as pinned entries (--pin-max). /health reports the cache.
- A tool call cut off at max_tokens is dropped and replaced with a note, instead
  of reaching the client as invalid JSON.
- When the last --repeat-call-guard turns made the same tool call and each one
  failed, the server adds a note and samples that turn at temperature 0.7.
---
